Method reference:
GaussianSlicer: Efficient Surface Reconstruction from Cross-sectional Slices
with Gaussian Splatting — Yuhu Guo, Chenghao Qian, Yuhong Mo, Akkarit Sangpetch.

Example contour provenance:
- examples/figure_eight: derived from OReX's eight_15.csl.
  https://github.com/haimsaw/OReX
  Source commit: 089db1f757022606399d5f070d65bd172fe69362
- examples/coronary: newly generated 75 parallel sections of
  coronary_arteries_v2.stl in the CrossSDF dataset.
  https://github.com/iamsalvatore/cross_sdf
  Source commit: c962cd2f7ee350cb5b6c78db592814901d1cf23c

Original data rights and terms remain with their respective owners. Sample arrays
derive solely from these contours. Reference meshes and the paper PDF are not
included. Results are generated by the implementation in this repository.

This code uses NumPy, SciPy, Shapely, PyTorch, scikit-image and trimesh through
their public APIs. Optional visualization uses PyVista/VTK, Matplotlib and Pillow.
Those packages are installed separately and retain their respective licenses.
